{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment to J5 (8efc61e7), adopted: J5's reliable catch-up is built as a scope entry stream that follows the read side of the Durable Streams protocol (https://github.com/durable-streams/durable-streams, PROTOCOL.md): catch-up GET ?offset, live=long-poll and live=sse, Stream-Next-Offset and Stream-Up-To-Date, ETag on immutable chunks. Appends are refused (405), so acts, their acceptance and idempotency stay exactly as they are; this is a read endpoint only.\n\nThe preparation note decides, before source:\n1. The offset format: entry seq, zero-padded so offsets sort as text (the archive already uses 12 digits); \"-1\" and \"now\" as the spec's sentinels.\n2. Who may read the entry stream and what each reader sees: the same authority and filtering as history/log reads; the session is re-checked before every send, as the current head stream does (sessions.ts:419-574). Off-the-shelf clients send Authorization: Bearer, so the stream accepts the session token that way; never in the URL.\n3. Framing: JSON mode of canonical entry lines, so readers can still verify the prev/hash chain and actor signatures themselves. The stream proves nothing on its own.\n4. Whether @durable-streams/server-conformance-tests can run against a read-only server, and which of its cases apply.\n\nThen move onto it: the head stream and its relay (packages/scope/src/sessions.ts streams), packages/client head-stream.ts and observe.ts, the MCP wait tool's one-second polling (packages/mcp/src/service.ts:913), and the room page's polling and manual refresh. \"Needs you\" and catch-up read from a stored offset (the \"mark reviewed\" point), which also serves J1's return from another device. Out of scope now: the protocol's webhook and pull-wake subscriptions (read them for J5's next step, notification and resumed agents) and the State Protocol. Done-when adds: the conformance cases that apply pass, and a reader that disconnects resumes from its offset with no gap and no duplicate."}